  perspective maybe an additional line of  dialogue which better explains events  those have been lucky enough to play the  game thus far have been shouting from  the rooftops about the depth of the  storytelling content available here as  an addition to the core plot like every  other great RPG you've played side  quests are here to add context and a  little catharsis to proceedings the plot  points from the anime which detract from  the main story have been hidden away in  plain sight  via character interactions in the game  but once again there's a curveball which  hardcore DBZ fans should know about  non-canon missions as we are in a fully  fleshed out world it's impossible to add  everything intended by writer Akira  Toriyama this is where there is a  distinct disconnect between the core  story and many side quests simply put  some of the side quests have been  invented especially for the game for  example there's a way to fish here and  how do we do it with Goku's tail if I  remember rightly it was cut off  permanent  but luckily he keeps it inside his  Jersey to bring out whenever he wants to  fish okay it's a bit strange but but  stick with it it's not exactly canon but  it's a great way to reintroduce elements  from the series which don't really play  an important part anymore because this  is an open world to some degree and time  passes within the game which is possible  to meet some characters earlier than  first suggested in the manga this will  introduce backstories to characters as  you see what they were like through sub  quests again keep in mind that these are  not necessarily canon but added  backstories which should help us  understand their choices later in the  story I've used the term open world a  couple of times already when asked if  the world is fully open the devs gave oh  yes no answer so to help clarify this  the world is indeed separated into huge  sections huge zones and planet regions  which are not all sewn together you  can't walk 