fed and  has a huge pool of health and is all set  with his explosive wave which produces  an area of effect damage bubble great  for taking down large groups of foes  Vegeta is more focused towards ki blasts  and ranged combat but he can get in  there and fight on the inside too if he  needs to but the others are better  suited to that so there's an element of  tactics the characters you choose here's  something very cool - no not all quests  found in the open world can be accessed  by Goku missions will be hidden away at  only certain playable characters can  attain how cool is that so keep your  eyes open in-game a quick character swap  could open up another storyline and more  precious RPG goodness in addition to  this Goku is able to take support  characters with him up to two to be  precise and just as we saw with the  playable characters each supporting  character has unique skills in battle  for example Crillon is able to use solar  flare to blind enemies alone Goku to run  up and start a combo on contest it the  answer has a way to restrict enemy  movement via his spirit ball he can also  gain aggro from enemies which could help  if you find yourself near death ciaossu  has telekinesis to restrain enemies Tien  is another with a saw  a flair but he also has a try beam for  straight-up damage the skill is to  choose the right duo to take into the  right fight because of the next key  point those characters will actually  think for themselves when in battle  think of them as autonomous or  ai-controlled  but no they are constantly learning how  you fight to improve their own reactions  in battle  the devs aren't giving us everything  right away and holding back on support  and playable characters but have  suggested more can be added in updates  and DLC if the community want that if  the name doesn't give it away already  the dragonballs can be found and  collected in-game which in turn summons  Sharon from here using our wishes we can  actually will a foreign enemy back to  life basically we can fight an enemy for  a second time but with new conditions  and much more difficult beating these  bosses will reward Goku with items and  skills which will make his journey a  little easier this aspect brings in  replayability and good old what-if  scenarios with additional dialogue from  each of the characters and speaking of  dialogue do you prefer Dragon Ball Z  Kakarot oh if it's the latter you should  know from minute one the audio can be  switched to Japanese making the world  feel even more authentic there are many  original voice actors returning which  makes this option unmissable for the  hardcore fans I sadly cannot read  subtitles quick enough here so I'll  stick with good old English there's an  unwritten rule and Dragon Ball Z games  are made a new character must be  designed this time around Dragon Ball  creator Akira Toriyama has returned to  the franchise to introduce a brand new  character especially for Dragon Ball Z  Kakarot will soon meet bond you who  looks like a thick girl so I'm all up  for this formerly one of the ginyu force  this beaut will appear in a short  training mission which can be opened  early if you pre-ordered the games  hmm ultimately this will make the game a  little easier as you'll have an ability  bar before you should obtain that in the  game naturally I'm not sure how I feel  about that well we've started looking  down pre-order bonuses so let's jump in  with both feet in two versions of the  game in addition to the standard edition  you have the collectors deluxe  Ultimate editions to choose from the  deluxe version includes a cooking item  which Awards permanent key attack and HP  boosts and the season pass which will  add two more original stories and one  new Canon story later in the games  lifecycle the Ultimate Edition has all  of that plus a music pack of eleven  freaking awesome anime trucks to get you  groove on - and the Tau pi PI pillar  from spring 2020 hmm interesting  